  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Manik Ruhidas & Ors vs Unknown on 18 May, 2016 Author: Joymalya Bagchi Bench: Joymalya Bagchi 93. 18.05.2016 C.R.R. 1644 of 2016 Aloke Ct. No.28 In the matter of : Manik Ruhidas & Ors. Mr. Sujan Chatterjee ... for the petitioner s Proceeding in the instant case being S.C. Case No. 137 (12) of 2015 pending before learned Sessions Judge, 3rd Court, Tamluk, Purba Medinipur arising out of Moyna P.S. Case No. 228 of 2015 under Sections 272/273 Ipc and Section 304/120B Ipc and Section 46Aa of the Bengal Excise Act and Section 16(3) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act has been challenged.",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "Mr. Chatterjee, learned counsel for the petitioners submits that the offence under Section 46AA of the Bengal Excise Act and Section 16(3) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act are triable by the learned Magistrate and, therefore, proceeding before the Court of Sessions is not maintainable.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Mr. Chatterjee, learned counsel for the petitioners submits that the offence under Section 46AA of the Bengal Excise Act and Section 16(3) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act are triable by the learned Magistrate and, therefore, proceeding before the Court of Sessions is not maintainable.",
